From d20a63d1f417a8fae54519ea5b41822524965c4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: r6c <r6c@local>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:53:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] status.IDLE_BUFF_HIT_TICK = client16402_off_on_hit_tick:
 the Evo Knight takes whole the hits landing on its own hit tick

Mechanic: combat.rs idle_on reads a unit's own idle buff at the tick's start state and state.rs idle_buff_pass moves it off
only after Resolve, so the hits landing on the tick of the Evo Knight's own hit were reduced by Knight_Fortify_EV1 (60).
New arm client16402_off_on_hit_tick (shipped): damage_reduction_of leaves the own idle buff out while the unit's attack
phase is Cooldown (the tick its hit lands), so every hit of that tick's Resolve is taken whole. Old arm start_of_tick;
CLIENT15535_ARMS keeps it (unread there), format-3 snapshots keep it. The Super Knight's area idle buff is not touched
(no own buff).

Minimal reproduction: tests/idle_buff_hit_tick.rs: a blue Evo Knight put down, a red Knight held out of sight until its
deploy ends and then put inside its reach, both kept and topped up: both first hits land on one tick; the Evo Knight takes
the red Knight's whole hit under the new arm and 40 % of it under the old. Plant idle_buff_reduces_own_hit_tick turns it red.

Parity-Evidence: ClashBot scratchpad/gauntlet/L74/parity/diag_night/r6c (ekhit.py) on the 359 captured client 16.402 frame
logs: Evo Knight engagements with the Knight_Fortify_EV1 row on before the windup and one enemy holding the Knight; in the 7
whose enemy's phase-3 attack progress equals the Knight's on every common tick of [hit - 8, hit + 2] (both hits on one tick:
Knight x5, Goblin Machine x2) the drop on that tick is the enemy's whole hit (293, 323, 323, 323, 293, 338, 338), where the
engine took 40 %. liveplay 20261017_050051 t3053: two Evo Knights, reduced until the frame before, take 293 and 323 off each
other on their common hit tick. 20261017_112814 t2042 and 20261017_111735 t3839: an Evo Mega Knight's 429 lands whole on our
Evo Knight's hit tick; the engine took 171.
